From 291afa9f28a7ab9af2d659b7048074c7c1932fe7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian MacDonald <ian@netstatz.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 01:12:46 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 052/109] fix: run the litert, tflite and executorch backends
 through start_server

Upstream replaced the raw process-handle API (start_process,
set_process_handle, wait_for_ready) with ServerProcess and
WrappedServer::start_server. The three fork backends now start their
subprocess the same way onnxruntime does, and unload() is stop_server().
start_server() keeps the exit status of a child that died before it was
ready, read from ServerProcess::exit_code(), so executorch still reports a
SIGKILL during load as a likely OOM without relaunching it.

Assisted-by: claude:opus-5.5
